1. Log in to your DNS provider's control panel (e.g., Route53 if you're using AWS).
2. Create an A record named `metablog` pointing to the IP address of your backend server (`0.0.0.0` for now).
3. Add another A record named `subdomain-to-target` pointing to the same IP address.
4. Ensure both records point to the same IP address for consistency.

### Step 2: Configure Your Backend Server

Your backend server should be configured to handle HTTPS requests. This typically involves setting up SSL certificates for HTTPS and configuring Nginx or Apache.

#### Example Configuration with Nginx:
```nginx
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name metablog.wrapperlabs.com;

    # SSL configuration
    ssl_certificate /path/to/certificate.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /path/to/privatekey.key;

    location / {
        proxy_pass https://meta-blog-381321.uc.r.appspot.com/;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }
}
```

### Step 3: Update Your Application Code

Make sure your application code redirects all traffic from `metablog.wrapperlabs.com` to the new URL provided
